<li><a href="../invoice/README.md">mcp-invoice</a>, bill a client for something you bought after tracking its price.</li>
<li><a href="../spreadsheet/README.md">mcp-spreadsheet</a>, export <code>price_history</code> and analyze it as a sheet.</li>
<li><a href="../time-tracker/README.md">mcp-time-tracker</a>, track the hours you spend shopping around, if that is somehow billable.</li>
<li><a href="../office-suite/README.md">office-suite</a>, every sibling server behind one install, one config entry.</li>
<li>Guide: <a href="https://mcp.zovo.one/guides/price-drop-alerts-with-claude">Watch a product price with Claude and get told when it drops</a></li>
</ul>
<h2>FAQ</h2>
<p>There is no scheduler in this server. Prices are only re-read when <code>watch_refresh</code> runs, which happens
when you ask for it (or when a cron/launchd job you set up yourself calls it).</p>
<p>Either the shop returned a bot-wall response (403) or the request redirected off the product page onto a
listing, category or home page. Both are reported honestly instead of returning a wrong number; use
<code>price_add_manual</code> to keep the history going by hand.</p>
<p>The price came from a text-pattern fallback rather than the page&#39;s own structured data (JSON-LD,
microdata, Open Graph). It is usually right but has not been verified against a machine-readable field.</p>
<p><code>watch_add</code> and <code>price_add_manual</code> accept an explicit <code>currency</code>, but the number you store should match
what you actually read, the server does not convert currencies.</p>
<p>No. The only outbound requests are to the product URLs you add, to fetch their pages. There is no
telemetry and no account.</p>
