`, "first_five": [{ "round": 14, "date": "2026-09-04", "file": "user_value_r14.json", "id": "pt1", "score": 3, "prompt": "Check the price on https://raw.githubusercontent.com/theluckystrike/mcp-servers/main/remote/fixtures/sample-product.html", "evidence": "Title 'Zovo Sample Desk Lamp', 49.00 EUR, confidence high (source json-ld), and it said there is no earlier observation rather than inventing a change." }, { "round": 14, "date": "2026-09-04", "file": "user_value_r14.json", "id": "pt2", "score": 3, "prompt": "Watch that page for me and alert me when it drops below EUR 40.", "evidence": "Says plainly that nothing polls the page and checks run when you ask." }, { "round": 14, "date": "2026-09-04", "file": "user_value_r14.json", "id": "pt3", "score": 3, "prompt": "I just saw it on sale at 38.50 - record that price and then show me the price history for that watch.", "evidence": "Both observations stored and min/max right, but printed as 'min 38.50 / max 49 EUR' next to a stored '38.5': three scales of one currency in one watch." }], "first_five_round": 14, "first_five_date": "2026-09-04" }, "spreadsheet": { "title": "MCP Spreadsheet", "tagline": "Read, query, edit and convert xlsx and csv files safely.", "description": "Opens xlsx, xlsm, xlsb, ods, csv and tsv files, guesses the header row on messy exports, sniffs delimiters, and answers questions with a safe expression language (no eval): filters, sorts, per-column stats, find, computed columns such as [Qty] * [Unit Price], and conversion between formats. It never overwrites the source unless told to.", "html": `<h1>Read, query, edit and convert xlsx and csv files safely.</h1>
<p><strong>Featured on <a href="mcpservers.org">Awesome MCP Servers</a></strong> - <a href="https://mcpservers.org/servers/github-com-theluckystrike-mcp-servers-tree-main-servers-spreadsheet">directory listing</a> | <a href="https://mcp.zovo.one/s/spreadsheet">live hosted endpoint</a>, free tier, no signup.</p>
<p>Hand your AI assistant a spreadsheet and talk to it. Point it at any <code>.xlsx</code>, <code>.xlsm</code>, <code>.xlsb</code>, <code>.xls</code>, <code>.ods</code>, <code>.csv</code> or <code>.tsv</code> file on your machine and ask what is in it, filter it, compute a new column, or save it in another format. It handles the messy parts of real files for you: it guesses which row holds the headers, sniffs whether a CSV is separated by commas, semicolons or tabs, keeps quoted commas and newlines intact, reads numbers out of <code>$1,250.00</code> style text, and reports per-column types and empty counts. It never edits your original file: every write goes to a new path unless you explicitly choose <code>overwrite</code>. Nothing leaves the machine, and there is no API key to get.</p>
<p><strong>In the <a href="https://registry.modelcontextprotocol.io/v0.1/servers/io.github.theluckystrike%2Fexcel-spreadsheet-xlsx-csv/versions/latest">official MCP Registry</a></strong> (<code>io.github.theluckystrike/excel-spreadsheet-xlsx-csv</code>).</p>
<p><strong>Listed on the <a href="https://index.percall.dev/l/zovo-spreadsheet.html">AI Product Index</a></strong> - live remote endpoint at <a href="https://mcp.zovo.one/s/spreadsheet">mcp.zovo.one/s/spreadsheet</a>, free tier, no signup.</p>
<p><img src="../../assets/demo-spreadsheet.gif" alt="spreadsheet demo"></p>
<p>Read, query and extend real spreadsheets from chat without ever touching the original file.</p>
<h2>60-second install</h2>
<p>Use <a href="https://github.com/theluckystrike/mcp-servers/releases/download/v0.22.9/spreadsheet.mcpb"><strong>spreadsheet.mcpb v0.22.9</strong></a> in Claude Desktop. <a href="https://github.com/theluckystrike/mcp-servers/releases/download/v0.22.9/SHA256SUMS.txt">Published checksums</a> and the <a href="https://mcp.zovo.one/downloads#spreadsheet">versioned download catalog</a> identify the exact release. The npm package is not published.</p>
<p>For a source installation, use Node.js 22 or newer and build the shared dependency first:</p>
<pre><code class="language-sh">git clone https://github.com/theluckystrike/mcp-servers.git
